1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,460
Theme blocks only work inside modern
Shopify themes.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:08,615
But sometimes you need a model in a blog
post, a legacy template, an email landing

3
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:11,256
page, or a site that isn't Shopify at all.

4
00:00:11,316 --> 00:00:12,765
That's what this is for.

5
00:00:13,975 --> 00:00:17,670
Open any library model and you'll find the
Share and embed card.

6
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:20,898
It gives you two things: a link, and an
iframe snippet.

7
00:00:21,758 --> 00:00:26,533
The viewer link is a real, public page
that renders just this model at full size.

8
00:00:26,593 --> 00:00:29,160
Anyone with the link can open it — no
login.

9
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:33,756
The ID is a random UUID so it isn't
guessable, and the page is marked noindex

10
00:00:33,816 --> 00:00:36,025
so it won't turn up in search results.

11
00:00:36,885 --> 00:00:37,866
Here's that page.

12
00:00:37,926 --> 00:00:42,584
Nothing but your model, filling the
window, with your saved settings applied.

13
00:00:42,644 --> 00:00:47,179
Send it to a client, drop it in a Slack
message, put it behind a QR code on

14
00:00:47,239 --> 00:00:47,839
packaging.

15
00:00:48,652 --> 00:00:51,619
The embed code wraps that same page in an
iframe.

16
00:00:51,679 --> 00:00:56,745
It's deliberately built to survive: every
style is inline, there are no CSS classes

17
00:00:56,805 --> 00:01:01,625
and no script tag, so Shopify's HTML
sanitiser leaves it alone and your theme's

18
00:01:01,685 --> 00:01:03,231
CSS can't collide with it.

19
00:01:04,091 --> 00:01:04,691
Two modes.

20
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:09,037
Responsive keeps a four-to-three box at
whatever width the column happens to be,

21
00:01:09,097 --> 00:01:12,820
which is what you want inside a page
layout you don't fully control.

22
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:16,475
Fixed pins the model's saved height in
pixels instead.

23
00:01:16,535 --> 00:01:20,018
Use it when you want the viewer exactly as
tall as you designed it.

24
00:01:20,878 --> 00:01:22,192
Three places it goes.

25
00:01:22,252 --> 00:01:27,492
A Shopify page or blog post — switch the
rich text editor to the HTML view first,

26
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:29,127
the angle-bracket button.

27
00:01:29,187 --> 00:01:34,427
A Custom Liquid section, which works in
every theme including legacy liquid ones.

28
00:01:34,487 --> 00:01:35,866
Or any website at all.

29
00:01:36,726 --> 00:01:38,601
Hit Copy and it's on your clipboard.

30
00:01:39,311 --> 00:01:42,674
And there it is, sitting in a blog post,
fully interactive.

31
00:01:42,734 --> 00:01:47,201
Your theme's typography above and below
it, the model in the middle, no layout

32
00:01:47,261 --> 00:01:47,861
fighting.

33
00:01:48,583 --> 00:01:49,693
Now the clever bit.

34
00:01:49,753 --> 00:01:54,743
Two settings can ride on the URL, so one
model can suit several placements without

35
00:01:54,803 --> 00:01:55,543
re-saving it.

36
00:01:55,603 --> 00:02:00,408
Question mark b g equals a hex colour
changes the background — and note there's

37
00:02:00,468 --> 00:02:03,672
no hash symbol, because a hash starts a
URL fragment.

38
00:02:03,732 --> 00:02:06,444
And autorotate equals zero stops it
spinning.

39
00:02:07,304 --> 00:02:11,517
Here's the same model, same saved
settings, with question mark b g equals

40
00:02:11,577 --> 00:02:15,556
one-oh-one-oh-one-four appended — sitting
comfortably on a dark page.

41
00:02:15,616 --> 00:02:20,180
Re-saving the model would have changed
every other placement; this changes only

42
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:20,840
this one.

43
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:25,481
One thing not to strip out: allow equals
fullscreen on the iframe tag.

44
00:02:25,541 --> 00:02:29,851
Without it, the browser refuses the
fullscreen request and the button appears

45
00:02:29,911 --> 00:02:30,646
to do nothing.

46
00:02:31,506 --> 00:02:35,782
Finally, the Preview button in the header
opens that public page in a tab.

47
00:02:35,842 --> 00:02:40,411
It renders the saved settings, so if
you've just changed something, save first.

48
00:02:41,271 --> 00:02:45,871
Next, we look at the viewer from the other
side — what your customer can actually do

49
00:02:45,931 --> 00:02:46,531
with it.
